But there's a subtlety: if wr side writes to mem[rd_bin] while rd side is holding rd_valid high (waiting for rd_ready), the data would change! But wait, if rd_valid is high, that means rd_bin != wr_bin_sync, so there's data at rd_bin that hasn't been read. The wr side can't write to that address because it would need to wrap around, which requires full. So the data at rd_bin is stable. Good.

